                <pb facs="0373" n="285" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg285"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Loomis to Mr.
                            Dawson.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1904-11-26"><hi rendition="#italic">November 26,
                        1904</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Loomis asks whether the refusal of the Dominican Government to put the
                    financial agent in charge of the custom houses at Monte Christi, Sanchez, and
                    Samana is final.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
